# --- Inter-session coordination (wp-workflow) ---
# Liveness heartbeats: one file per session, rewritten on every poll of that session's
# log watch. Its whole signal is the mtime, and git does not store mtime — a tree object
# carries mode, type, sha and name, nothing else. On clone every file gets the checkout
# time, so a committed heartbeat comes back looking freshly touched and asserts that a
# long-dead session is alive. "No heartbeat means unknown, never dead" is only safe while
# a heartbeat that IS present cannot lie.
docs/coordination/heartbeat/

# NOTE: docs/coordination/log.md is deliberately NOT listed here. Whether the log is
# tracked is a per-project decision (see bootstrap.md); the heartbeat directory is not —
# it is runtime state under every storage mode.
